 **Objective score for this run.** This run has a single objective, the AppWorld task reward: 1.0 if every AppWorld test of the task passes, else 0.0. The harness scores a candidate by the mean reward over the 147 optimization tasks, one trial each, and accepts it only if the mean paired gain over the current best clears its noise gate. Partial passes earn nothing; the failed-requirement texts in each trajectory say which checks failed. There are no other components (no cost or length objective).
 
 The candidate is three files; nothing else is read by the agent under test:
-- `policy/instructions.txt` — the ReAct prompt (capability system-prompt). A Jinja template
-  rendered with `instruction`, `main_user`, `app_descriptions` ONLY, split into chat messages
-  on `USER:` / `ASSISTANT:` lines. Keep that structure, keep the worked demo format (one
-  ```python block per ASSISTANT turn), and keep the final block
-  `My name is: … Task: {{ instruction }}` last. At most 8,000 tokens.
 - `tools/helpers.py` — plain Python functions (capability tools), executed once in the agent's
   REPL before step 1. They are NOT model tools: the agent calls them from its own code, e.g.
   `items = fetch_all_pages(apis, "spotify", "show_playlist_library", access_token=t)`. Rules
